==Faroese==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fo}} {{m|non|elska}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*aliskaną||to care for, cultivate, cherish}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*aliskaz||dear, precious}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fo}} {{m|gem-pro|*al-||to spur, drive, be enthusiastic}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fo}} {{m|ine-pro|*el-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*lā-||to drive, move, go}}.

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|elskaði|elskaðu|elskað}}

# to [[love]]
#* ''[[eg elski teg|Eg '''elski''' teg]].''
#*: I love you.
#* ''[[antin|Antin]] '''elskar''' [[tú]] [[tað]], [[ella]] [[hata]]r tú tað.''
#*: Either you love it or you hate it.

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-30|elsk}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|fo|hata}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|fo|unna}}, {{l|fo|ynna}}, {{l|fo|alska}}

