==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|elska}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛlska/|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|elsku|elskur}}

# [[love]]
#: ''Ekki gráta '''elsku''' vinur.''
#:: Don't cry '''dear''' friend.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1||e|lsk|n=?}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|elskan mín}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|elskaði|elskað}}

# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|with accusative}} to [[love]]{{jump|love|s}}
#: ''Ég '''elska''' konuna mína.''
#:: I '''love''' my wife.
#: ''Hann '''elskaði''' mig aldrei.''
#:: He never '''loved''' me.

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w4||e|lsk}}

====Usage notes====
* The verb '''elska''' is mostly used about people and animals or pets (though rarely). Almost never used about inanimate things such as food, cars etc.

====Derived terms====
* [[ég elska þig]]
* [[elskast]]

====Synonyms====
* {{jump|s|love}} [[unna]]

